      {
        "id": 64487,
        "name": "arenson9",
        "username": "arenson9",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arenson9/{size}/1900_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-05-28T01:13:44.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>There are situations where the rules for a card/villain say to do things like \"reveal until X something-or-other cards are found. Put them into play. Discard the other revealed cards\".</p><p>In general, however, the standard definition of discard is used: Cards go from hand to trash.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>It's an unfortunately ambiguous glossary definition. It would be better if it explicitly said something like \"unless otherwise stated, 'to discard' means to move a card from hand to trash\".</p>",
        "post_number": 3,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:41:40.234Z",
