        "raw": "<p>There are situations where the rules for a card/villain say to do things like &quot;reveal until X something-or-other cards are found. Put them into play. Discard the other revealed cards&quot;.</p><p>In general, however, the standard definition of discard is used: Cards go from hand to trash.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>It&#39;s an unfortunately ambiguous glossary definition. It would be better if it explicitly said something like &quot;unless otherwise stated, &#39;to discard&#39; means to move a card from hand to trash&quot;.</p>",
